218-/** Re-load the active sheet so the screen shows what the store holds now. Loading the same id
219- *  again is not observable (the current id already reads that), so the screen first loads a
220- *  throwaway id, which has no one on it, and waits for the person rows to go; then it loads the
221- *  sheet again and waits for rows to show. Rows that were on screen before may rightly not come
222- *  back (someone retired since, say), so the wait is for any row, and for every row that is back
223- *  to carry at least the claims it had; if none shows within the wait the screen is taken as it
224- *  is and the test's own checks decide. The show-retired box and the as-of date, which belong to
225- *  the screen, are put back if the loads reset them. */
